{{- /* Single source of truth for "can we read from Proton Pass right now?".
       Renders the literal string "true" or "false", same convention as
       is-container and is-devpod-platform.

       lookPath returns "" rather than failing when the binary is absent, which
       is the container case: .chezmoiexternals/pass-cli.toml is host-only.

       `pass-cli info` is the session test, wrapped in `sh -c … && echo true ||
       echo false` because chezmoi's `output` aborts the whole template on a
       non-zero exit — the very failure this gate exists to prevent. Wrapped, sh
       always exits 0 and the template gets a string. */ -}}
{{- if lookPath "pass-cli" -}}
{{- output "sh" "-c" "pass-cli info >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo true || echo false" | trim -}}
{{- else -}}false{{- end -}}
